<title>GERMANY: German traders make no intvn grain export bids.</title>
<headline>German traders make no intvn grain export bids.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders showed no interest in exporting intervention grain under this week's European Union grain export tender, state intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BLE received no bids for intervention grain.</p>
<p>Traders were concentrating on the transport of volumes released in earlier tenders and on exports of free market grain, a BLE source said.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
